+// behind it. The Figma Footer component has exactly three size variants (Mobile 320–767, Tablet
+// 768–1023, Desktop 1024+), confirmed by the UI designer against the comps' own min/max widths.
+// It was also actively harmful: the nav columns reach their natural width around 836px, but at
+// 860px that rule spent 40px more on gaps than the row had, squeezing them back below their
+// content width and re-wrapping labels that had just recovered. Measured across 768–1024 in 2px
+// steps against a built Storybook, removing it takes the broken span from ~124px to ~68px of the
+// 256px tablet band. Do not add a fourth breakpoint without a matching Figma variant.
